      "body": "I don't think #34897 fully fixed this issue. I am able to reproduce this with the following LLM-generated functional test:\n\n<details>\n<summary>test</summary>\n\n```\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n# Copyright (c) 2026-present The Bitcoin Core developers\n# Distributed under the MIT software license, see the accompanying\n# file COPYING or http://www.opensource.org/licenses/mit-license.php.\n\"\"\"Test that the block filter index survives a reorg followed by an unclean shutdown.\n\nThe block filter index writes its height-keyed records eagerly, in\nBlockFilterIndex::Write, rather than through the deferred BaseIndex::Commit\nbatch. So after a reorg the record at a given height holds the new branch's\nblock even if the chainstate never flushed. An unclean shutdown then rolls the\nchainstate back to the last flushed tip, and on the next start\nBlockFilterIndex::CustomInit reads the height record for that restored tip,\nfinds the other branch's block there, and fails fatally:\n\n    [error] previous block header belongs to unexpected block <new>; expected <restored>\n    [error] Cannot read last block filter header; index may be corrupted\n\nThe node then cannot start again without a reindex.\n\nThe filter for the restored tip is not lost -- BlockFilterIndex::CustomRemove\ncopies it to the hash index before the height record is overwritten -- so the\ninit path can recover it via index_util::LookUpOne, which already implements\nexactly that height-then-hash fallback.\n\nRelated: bitcoin#34261, which PR bitcoin#34897 only fixed for indexes whose\nstate goes through Commit() (coinstatsindex).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom test_framework.test_framework import BitcoinTestFramework\nfrom test_framework.util import assert_equal\n\n# Blocks on the branch that gets flushed, and on the branch that replaces it.\n# The second branch only has to be longer than the first.\nFLUSHED_BRANCH_LEN = 10\nREORG_BRANCH_LEN = 12\n\n\nclass BlockFilterIndexReorgUncleanShutdownTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\n    def set_test_params(self):\n        self.num_nodes = 2\n        self.setup_clean_chain = True\n        # node0 carries the index and is the one that gets killed. node1 only\n        # exists to hand it a competing branch.\n        self.extra_args = [[\"-blockfilterindex=1\"], []]\n\n    def setup_network(self):\n        # Connected on demand: the two branches have to be mined in isolation.\n        self.setup_nodes()\n\n    def wait_for_index(self, node):\n        \"\"\"Wait until the block filter index has caught up with the node's tip.\"\"\"\n        node.syncwithvalidationinterfacequeue()\n        self.wait_until(lambda: node.getindexinfo(\"basic block filter index\")\n                        [\"basic block filter index\"][\"best_block_height\"] == node.getblockcount())\n\n    def run_test(self):\n        node, helper = self.nodes\n\n        self.log.info(\"Mine the branch that will be flushed to disk\")\n        self.generate(node, FLUSHED_BRANCH_LEN, sync_fun=self.no_op)\n        self.wait_for_index(node)\n        flushed_tip = node.getbestblockhash()\n\n        self.log.info(\"Mine a longer competing branch on the helper node\")\n        self.generate(helper, REORG_BRANCH_LEN, sync_fun=self.no_op)\n        reorg_tip = helper.getbestblockhash()\n        assert flushed_tip != reorg_tip\n\n        # A clean shutdown is what makes the chainstate and the index durable at\n        # the same point. Everything after this restart is unflushed.\n        self.log.info(\"Restart cleanly, so chainstate and index are durable at this tip\")\n        self.restart_node(0)\n        assert_equal(node.getbestblockhash(), flushed_tip)\n\n        self.log.info(\"Reorg onto the competing branch, without a chainstate flush\")\n        self.connect_nodes(0, 1)\n        self.sync_blocks()\n        assert_equal(node.getbestblockhash(), reorg_tip)\n        # The index follows the reorg and overwrites its height records with the\n        # new branch's blocks, copying the displaced ones to the hash index.\n        self.wait_for_index(node)\n\n        # Nothing below may reconnect or re-announce the reorged branch.\n        self.disconnect_nodes(0, 1)\n        self.stop_node(1)\n\n        self.log.info(\"Kill the node before it can flush the reorg\")\n        node.kill_process()\n\n        self.log.info(\"Restart: the node must come back on the last flushed tip\")\n        # On the buggy build this start fails with \"Cannot read last block\n        # filter header; index may be corrupted\" and the node exits 1.\n        self.start_node(0)\n        assert_equal(node.getbestblockhash(), flushed_tip)\n\n        self.log.info(\"The index must still serve the restored tip's filter\")\n        node.getblockfilter(flushed_tip)\n        self.wait_for_index(node)\n        assert_equal(node.getindexinfo(\"basic block filter index\")\n                     [\"basic block filter index\"][\"best_block_height\"], FLUSHED_BRANCH_LEN)\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    BlockFilterIndexReorgUncleanShutdownTest(__file__).main()\n```\n\n</details>\n\nThe logs of node0 show the exact logs in the OP on 228877d7836a55c1d6fde90b0b7ba2d4c90248ab.\n\nRan into this with fuzzamoto + bedrock.",
